# Formerly pinned 0 1 0, seen 1 by the rule R89, opening is an attempt (the author 2026-11-18): the one field of
# S would take the formal v the whole took, so nothing was opened. TZ 2026-11-19 §9.3 withdraws it («W и E
# равноправны»): W -- S whole to `@: v M` (M empty) -- and E -- the field `@: v Inner`, v := Inner -- both fit
# the one declaration: two candidates, ambiguity 3 (§9.8, the row «W и E подходят одному объявлению»); nothing
# runs, seen 0. Derived before the run (opus, step 21.5; fable Р130).
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
)

sub: main (M(); Inner(int: x 1; int: y 2); S(@: v Inner))
    @: shared node[0]
    fn: f (@: v M) int
        return: length(v)
    shared\Observed\seen := f(S)
main()
